Server ticks ran 1.49x the local figure (156,535 vs 104,833).

Entry packing was investigated and is DOMINATED here — recorded so nobody
retries it. Entries are -99..99, so 8 bits each and 8 per 64-bit word, but
matmul's tape holds only 14 scalars and a tape is 32x32 whatever N is; the
matrices live in the STREAM block's pipe rings. Sweeping STREAM_SIZE
257/129/65/33/17/9/5/3 gives 8100 -> 7744 and then nothing: below 129 slots
the WIDTH binds, and the width is the tape's, not the rings'. So 8-per-word
buys exactly what 2-per-word buys, and a pipe re-route collects it for free.

An independent 88x87 (area2 7744) fold exists on worktree-agent-a0b68d072175e6372
at 118,638 local ticks. It is complementary to this grid's tick work: combining
them should give 86x87, area2 7569, ~104,833 ticks, ~7.9e8 local. Merging
conflicts in machine.py and test_lm1_matmul.py.
